WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.270
<b>The fire calls
the wind.</b>

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.270
<b>Quiet in the library!</b>

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.570
<b>And the wind
becomes a storm.</b>

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.860
<b>Memories the color
 of twilight.</b>

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:15.400
Do you think you can beat my 
Gien in a close-quarters fight?

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.660
Th-This isn't just a card game?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.870
It is.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.160
But it's a bloody death game, too.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.260
N-Nobody told me that!

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.170
You summoned me without even knowing that?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:36.860
You usually don't expect to be 
caught up in something like this!

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.510
You're hurt!

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.930
Don't worry about me. Worry about yourself.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.810
A general depletes the 
spiritual power of their lord

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.460
as they act.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.280
If Shuuyu is injured,

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.110
your spiritual power decreases.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.110
It's only natural.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.360
Does that mean it whittles away at my life?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.180
Then if I run out?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.720
Looks like you drew a bad one,

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.720
Shuuyu Koukin!

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.350
A bad one?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.230
What does he mean?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.310
Tell me!

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.310
Time for a quiz, then.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.000
Shuuyu is a historical hero

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.320
who has defeated many enemies.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.320
Why is she having such a hard time?

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.570
Chose one of the following three options.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:50.080
One: She's just having a bad day.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.080
Two: She didn't get enough sleep.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.840
Three: Her lord's spiritual power is so low

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.840
that it's pathetic!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.480
This feels great.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.480
You students are little brats,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.990
and I've always hated you.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.990
N-No...

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:44.760
Gien, that's enough.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.010
Stand, Shuuyu.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.240
There's no need

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.450
for a general of your talents to 
serve a talentless lord forever.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.270
An ancient proverb says that a wise 
bird chooses the tree where it sleeps.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.390
There's nothing wrong with it at all.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:04.030
You don't want to go back

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.240
to that empty world, do you?

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.540
Pick up that blade.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.410
And chop off your lord's head,

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.600
to show your loyalty to me.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.490
I don't care if you want my lord's corpse.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.310
But...

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.410
You'll have

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.140
to cross over my own corpse first!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.800
Retsuouken!

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.160
<b>Retsuouken</b>

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.170
Damn it!

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.720
She hid with Sonshin?

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.060
Where did they go?

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.180
That skill was amazing.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.360
Why did you hide it?

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.360
Those big skills drain a 
lot of spiritual power.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.850
I can only manage to fire one more.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.870
If I miss, I won't even 
have the strength to run.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.630
No...

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:40.370
Hide-and-seek class is over.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.320
Fuurou no Jin!

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.130
<b>Fuurou no Jin</b>

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.750
Hey, are you okay?

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.950
Now you have nowhere else to hide, huh?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.670
<i>This is bad...</i>

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.660
<i>At this rate we're both dead!</i>

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.760
So you chose to die with 
your talentless lord?

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.520
This way!

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.020
Find them!

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.360
Don't let them out of the building.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.440
<b>Science Prep Room</b>

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.840
How could you run away?

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.940
Shh!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.730
They'll find us!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.450
You would've lost that fight!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.610
I do not fear death!

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.700
I do!

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.150
Jeez...

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:03.720
What a good-for-nothing lord I ended up with.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.770
Here. Let me see your arm.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.800
I told you not to worry about it.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.710
Just do it!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.240
There...

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.100
I hope this restores some of 
that spiritual power stuff.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:18.220
Again?

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:21.230
You don't like the twilight?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.980
Every time I lose a fight,

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:27.230
for some reason, it's always twilight.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.230
It seems to have it out for me.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:35.300
So you've fought battles like this before?

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.990
I've never run into a good-for-nothing 
like you before, though.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.510
You're generals from the <i>Romance 
of the Three Kingdoms</i>, right?

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.500
Why did you get turned into cards?

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.060
Does it have something to 
do with that empty world

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.900
that Sensei was talking about?

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.040
Our souls were ripped from our bodies

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.770
and locked away by a mysterious power...

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.720
In a place of accursed reincarnation.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.270
A place of reincarnation?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.770
All we can do there is wait 
for our turn to fight.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.560
We are eternally prevented from being reborn.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.280
We simply wait and wait...

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.710
For the time when we are called.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.790
That's no different than 
being a prisoner, though!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.070
My desire is to break this 
cursed cycle of reincarnation,

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.800
and find my final death.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.770
That's all.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.150
We're going to have to do all we can to run.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:40.440
Don't just decide that!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.380
I don't care what you say.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.400
Your lord's orders are absolute, right?

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.200
Who told you that?

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.310
You can disobey me?

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.260
I will happily kill an unrighteous lord.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.200
<b>Quiet in the hallways!</b>

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:03.320
We can't set fire to the building 
and escape in the chaos?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.810
If we do that, we'll get other 
people caught up in this.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.970
What's wrong with that?

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.460
There are always casualties in wars!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.380
Absolutely not!

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.960
You're a strange man.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.160
The school rules say that students have

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:18.970
to leave their phones in the teachers' 
office at the start of school.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.130
If I can just get mine back...

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.080
Phones?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.800
Just come with me!

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:28.000
Hello, Sonshin-kun.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.850
Is this what you're looking for?

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.520
Oops. Sorry.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:40.680
Go!

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:41.910
Right!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:50.170
You're a bad student 
for disobeying your teacher.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:53.420
I have to punish you.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.340
This way!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.170
Hey, it's a dead end!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:03.210
If we use the emergency stairs,
we can get outside.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.760
Damn it!

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:14.680
Anything you can think of, I can think of.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.360
This is a good place to die, isn't it,

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.360
Sonshin-kun?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.960
<b>Fin</b>

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.280
The sun sets in the sky.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.950
The flame is buffeted by the wind.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.990
A false sky shrouds the high place,

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.980
barring the path.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.240
Danger approaches,

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.040
or perhaps, salvation.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:17.760
When the sun sets, a single crimson 
light comes down from the sky.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.590
Next time: "Twilight."
